abstract: >
  Nepal receives remittances equivalent to over 25% of GDP, yet agricultural
  productivity has stagnated across much of the country. This study examines
  whether migration-intensive districts are associated with below-average
  agricultural yields, using district-level cross-sectional data linking CBS
  Nepal 2021 Census migration indicators with MoALD 2022/23 cereal yield data
  across all 75 districts.
